- T1: Create spec file and quickstart (specs\\102-audit-menu-102-manage-wlan-radius-timers/spec.md) — 0.5d
  - Deliverable: spec, sample CSV schema, example .env defaults.

- T2: Implement WLANRadiusTimerManager class and manage() entrypoint in src (new file src/config/wlan_radius_timer_manager.py or under src/agents) — 2.5d
  - Subtasks:
    - Fetch org WLANs (listOrgWlans) and filter RADIUS-enabled.
    - Display numbered preview list, with template_id and current timer values.
    - Selection parser for flexible input (re-use src/input utilities if any).

- T3: Implement update logic (site WLAN updates and template updates) — 2d
  - Subtasks:
    - For site WLANs: call appropriate update site WLAN API with new timer values.
    - For template-managed: implement template modification path (explicit confirmation required).
    - Skip WLANs already matching target values.

- T4: Implement CSV export and logging — 1d
  - Create CSV writer following other export patterns (e.g. specs/001-radius-wlan-config CSV columns).
  - Ensure errors and successes captured per row.

- T5: Integrate rate limiting/retry and error handling — 0.5d
  - Reuse MistHelper utilities for retries.

- T6: Tests & CI — 1d
  - Unit tests for selection parser, diff computation; integration test with mocked API.
  - Add tests under tests/ with fixtures and use test_input.txt or mocks.

- T7: Documentation & release notes — 0.5d
  - Update menu registry, add help text and sample runs to README or docs.

Estimated total: ~8 days (can be reduced by reusing existing utilities in repo).